# ── The app ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave these unset and the app runs entirely on-device: every screen works,
# nothing is sent anywhere, and signing in accepts any six digits. That is the
# development and demo mode, and it is the mode the on-device tester ships in.
#
# Set them and the same code paths reconcile against Supabase — auth, the log
# queue's drain, pull sync and the live room's realtime channel all attach
# without a single screen changing.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google Places, for venue search and the "Open now" filter.
#
# Without it venues come from OpenStreetMap, which is complete enough to use and
# carries opening hours as free text this app will not guess at — so the
# Open-now chip correctly hides itself rather than filtering nothing.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLACES_KEY=

# Google sign-in. Per platform, because the client ids are.
#
# Unset, the Google button does not appear. It used to be worse than that: the
# sign-in screen rendered a blank page, because the auth-session hook throws
# during render when it has no client id for the platform it is on.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=

# ── The server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are NOT app variables. They are edge-function secrets, set with
# `supabase secrets set` or pushed by .github/workflows/supabase.yml, and they
# must never reach a client bundle — anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ does.
#
#   APNS_KEY_ID, APNS_TEAM_ID, APNS_PRIVATE_KEY
#       Live Activity updates. Without them the shared HUD never moves for
#       anybody but the person who logged the drink.
#
#   FCM_SERVER_KEY
#       Android push.
#
#   SMS_PROVIDER_SID, SMS_PROVIDER_TOKEN, SMS_FROM
#       The safe-arrival SMS. Without these the escalation stages a message and
#       has no way to send it — which is the one failure in this list that
#       matters at 3am.
#
#   STORE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#       What store-webhook authenticates itself against; it has no Supabase
#       session, so this is the whole check.
#
#   INVITE_PAGE_URL
#       Where the invite function fetches its page template from.

# ── Verifying a deployment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `npm run verify:deploy` reads this one. It is the direct Postgres connection
# string from Supabase's dashboard (Project Settings -> Database -> URI), and it
# is a superuser credential for your project — keep it out of the repo and out
# of anything with EXPO_PUBLIC_ in the name.
#
# The script checks the two steps docs/deploy.md warns are silent when skipped:
# pg_cron present and all seven jobs actually scheduled, and the outbound drain
# actually delivering rather than merely scheduled.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=
